# Firebase Admin Configuration
# ==================================
# Required for Firebase Storage to work in Firebase App Hosting
# Copy this to your Firebase App Hosting environment variables

# 🔴 CRITICAL: Firebase Service Account JSON
# How to get it:
# 1. Go to Firebase Console: https://console.firebase.google.com
# 2. Click Project Settings (gear icon)
# 3. Go to "Service Accounts" tab
# 4. Click "Generate New Private Key"
# 5. Copy the ENTIRE content of the downloaded JSON file
# 6. Paste it here (no spaces, keep it as ONE LINE in production)
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON='{"type":"service_account","project_id":"gen-lang-client-0364375301","private_key_id":"xxxxx","private_key":"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nMIIEvQIBADANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQE...-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n","client_email":"firebase-adminsdk-xxxxx@gen-lang-client-0364375301.iam.gserviceaccount.com","client_id":"1234567890","auth_uri":"https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth","token_uri":"https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token","auth_provider_x509_cert_url":"https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v1/certs","client_x509_cert_url":"https://www.googleapis.com/robot/v1/metadata/x509/firebase-adminsdk-xxxxx%40gen-lang-client-0364375301.iam.gserviceaccount.com"}'

# ✅ OPTIONAL but RECOMMENDED: Firebase Storage Bucket Name
# If not set, will be derived from project_id as: project-id.appspot.com
# Format: project-id.appspot.com (NOT https://...)
FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=gen-lang-client-0364375301.appspot.com

# ============================================
# VERIFICATION CHECKLIST
# ============================================
# After setting these variables, verify:
#
# ✅ Step 1: Check Firebase Console
#    - Storage → Browser
#    - You should see your storage bucket
#
# ✅ Step 2: Enable Google Cloud Storage API
#    - https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/storage-api.googleapis.com
#    - Click "Enable"
#
# ✅ Step 3: Grant IAM Permissions
#    - https://console.cloud.google.com/iam-admin/iam
#    - Find: firebase-adminsdk-xxxxx@[project-id].iam.gserviceaccount.com
#    - Add Roles:
#      • Storage Object Creator
#      • Storage Object Viewer
#
# ✅ Step 4: Deploy and test
#    - Upload image from Admin Gallery
#    - Check Firebase Console Storage
#    - Restart app and verify image persists
#
# ============================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING
# ============================================
#
# Error: "FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON is not set"
# → Solution: Copy the entire service account JSON from Firebase Console
#
# Error: "Invalid Firebase service account: missing required fields"
# → Solution: Make sure you copied the complete JSON file
#
# Error: "Permission denied"
# → Solution: Add IAM roles to the service account
#
# Error: "Invalid storage bucket"
# → Solution: Use format "project-id.appspot.com" (no https://)
#
# Images disappear after restart
# → Solution: Check if Firebase is configured (look for logs in Cloud Logging)
#
# ============================================
# CLOUD LOGGING
# ============================================
#
# To debug in Firebase App Hosting:
# 1. Go to Firebase Console → Functions → Logs
# 2. Look for messages like:
#    - "[Storage] Firebase Storage upload successful" ✅
#    - "[Storage] Firebase Storage failed" ❌
#
# Or use Google Cloud Logging:
# https://console.cloud.google.com/logs
